#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""THE WORLD TODAY -- front page for Saturday 21 November 2026.

One self-contained stdlib program. It paints a 1024x1024 newspaper page
with a tiny raster engine (rectangles, lines, discs, polygons, clipped
picture boxes) and bitmap text, then writes a single PNG. No network,
no files read at run time, no randomness: the same input always yields
the same bytes.

Run:  python3 main.py [output-path]
The output path defaults to $MAKEFUN_OUTPUT_DIR (a directory, in which
case entry.png is created inside it, or a full .png path), and finally
to /output/entry.png when neither an argument nor the variable is set.
"""

